EXTERNAL runEvent(eventId)

- Amelia: Well now, look what the road dragged in! You look half-starved. Tonight’s special is rabbit stew with garden vegetables, bread fresh from the oven,
<> and mead—hot or cold, depending on how bold you’re feeling.

* [Buy items]  
~ runEvent("Buy items from Amelia")  

* [What’s your story?]

Amelia: You mean how I ended up a tavern owner? I married one. Then one morning he decided he was tired of the married life, claimed there were better catches in the sea, and off he went. Never saw him again.

Amelia: I won’t pretend I’m easy to live with—hot-headed, stubborn, sharper than most men care for. Still, I kept the place for myself.
<> Turns out I’m better at keeping the fire lit, the ale flowing, and hot-blooded fools from splitting each other’s skulls before dessert.

Amelia: Adventure? I could’ve chased it. But why wander the wilds when the whole world eventually stumbles through my door?

* [Rumors]
{shuffle:  
    - Amelia: Word is, a blue-haired prince’s been locked away in a tower up in Mountainpass. Trouble always brews in that cursed pass.  

    - Amelia: The King’s ordered an audit of the army. Every soldier is walking on eggshells... it's a bad month for the tavern, as you might guess.

    - Amelia: Orcs near town? Hells, let them come—so long as they’ve got gold. Muddy boots in my hall, though… that’ll cost extra.
}

* [Goodbye]
